doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23108188"
# Concept DOI (all versions): 10.5281/zenodo.22950552
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked conditional reconstructions of arguments in the Surangama
  Sutra (Taisho T19 no. 945) in Lean 4. Version 0.2.1 provides seven standalone
  C1-C7 modules with numbered descriptive filenames and 49 theorem declarations,
  including branch lemmas and
  premise-scope witnesses, alongside the preserved v0.1.0 Core models.
  Premises are explicit theorem parameters or structure fields, not global
  doctrinal axioms. The release includes axiom-dependency reports and
  reproducible Boolean consistency and single-premise-omission checks.
  Selected routes, not every sentence or commentary reading, are formalized.
  Kernel checking does not establish premise truth, unique interpretation,
  empirical consciousness claims or an ontology of Buddha/Tathagatagarbha.
  Development was AI-assisted (Claude, Anthropic; Codex, OpenAI) under human
  direction; the author remains responsible for readings and claim boundaries.
